meta {
  name: Initialize
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/mcp
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{mcpUsername}}
  password: {{mcpPassword}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 1,
    "method": "initialize",
    "params": {
      "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
      "capabilities": {},
      "clientInfo": { "name": "bruno", "version": "1.0.0" }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  MCP handshake for the read-only agent endpoint. Every request to `/api/mcp` is a
  JSON-RPC 2.0 POST and must carry both headers above — the transport rejects a
  request that does not accept `text/event-stream`.

  **Basic auth, not Bearer.** This route is mounted before `authMiddleware` because
  MCP clients cannot run D-Pilot's login flow. Present the MCP service account's
  username/password as HTTP Basic (`{{mcpUsername}}` / `{{mcpPassword}}`); the route
  exchanges them for a normal JWT internally, so capability checks, PHI masking and
  audit logging all apply as usual.

  Stateless — no session id is issued, so `GET` and `DELETE` on this path return 405.
}
